{"name":"Rice Pudding","hex":"#fff0e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rice pudding","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A milk pudding made from rice, milk, sugar and nutmeg."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rice_pudding"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rice pudding","blocks":[{"text":"Rice pudding is a dish made from rice and milk, and commonly other ingredients such as sweeteners, spices, flavourings and sometimes eggs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Kheer_with_condensed_milk..JPG/330px-Kheer_with_condensed_milk..JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rice_pudding","wikidata":"Q19029"},{"title":"Rice","blocks":[{"text":"Rice is a cereal grain and, in its domesticated form, is the staple food of over half of the world's population, particularly in Africa and Asia. Rice is the seed of the grass species Oryza sativa —or, less commonly, Oryza glaberrima. Asian rice was domesticated in China some 13,500 to 8,200 years ago; African rice was domesticated independently in West Africa about 3,000 years ago. Rice has become commonplace in many cultures worldwide; in 2023, 800 million tons were produced, placing it third after sugarcane and maize. Only some 8% of rice is traded internationally. China, India, and Indonesia are the largest consumers of rice. A substantial amount of the rice produced in developing nations is lost after harvest through factors such as poor transport and storage. Rice yields can be reduced by pests including insects, rodents, and birds, as well as by weeds, and by diseases such as rice blast. Traditional rice polycultures such as rice-duck farming, and modern integrated pest management seek to control damage from pests in a sustainable way."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/20201102.Hengnan.Hybrid_rice_Sanyou-1.6.jpg/330px-20201102.Hengnan.Hybrid_rice_Sanyou-1.6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rice","wikidata":"Q5090"},{"title":"Pudding","blocks":[{"text":"Pudding is a food which can either be a dessert or a savoury dish. In the United States, pudding means a sweet, milk-based dessert similar in consistency to egg-based custards, instant custards or a mousse, often commercially set using cornstarch, gelatin or similar coagulating agent. These puddings are known in some Commonwealth countries as custards if they are egg-thickened, as blancmange if starch-thickened, and as jelly if gelatin-based. Pudding in America may also refer to other dishes such as bread pudding and rice pudding, although typically these names derive from their origin as British dishes. The modern American meaning of pudding as dessert has evolved from the original almost exclusive use of the term to describe savoury dishes, specifically those created using a process similar to that used for sausages, in which meat and other ingredients in mostly liquid form are encased and then steamed or boiled to set the contents."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Blanc-manger_on_glass_platter%2C_full_view.jpg/330px-Blanc-manger_on_glass_platter%2C_full_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pudding","wikidata":"Q9053"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Arros_amb_llet.jpg/500px-Arros_amb_llet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Arros_amb_llet.jpg/1280px-Arros_amb_llet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Arros_amb_llet.jpg/500px-Arros_amb_llet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Arroz con leche (rice with milk) is the Spanish and American type of rice pudding. Leftover rice is often used, especially in restaurants.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArros_amb_llet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Firinda_s%C3%BCtla%C3%A7.jpg/500px-Firinda_s%C3%BCtla%C3%A7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Firinda_s%C3%BCtla%C3%A7.jpg/1280px-Firinda_s%C3%BCtla%C3%A7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Firinda_s%C3%BCtla%C3%A7.jpg/500px-Firinda_s%C3%BCtla%C3%A7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Turkish fırın sütlaç, baked","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFirinda_s%C3%BCtla%C3%A7.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Lebanesericepudding.JPG/500px-Lebanesericepudding.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Lebanesericepudding.JPG/1280px-Lebanesericepudding.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Lebanesericepudding.JPG/500px-Lebanesericepudding.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lebanese riz bi haleeb","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALebanesericepudding.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Kheer_Rice_Pudding_Indian_Sweet_Buffalo_New_York.jpg/500px-Kheer_Rice_Pudding_Indian_Sweet_Buffalo_New_York.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Kheer_Rice_Pudding_Indian_Sweet_Buffalo_New_York.jpg/1280px-Kheer_Rice_Pudding_Indian_Sweet_Buffalo_New_York.j